{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-028",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 28,
  "title": "Job 28",
  "display_title": "Job 28",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 28,
  "sortOrder": 18028,
  "verseCount": 28,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Surely there is a vein for the silver, and a place for gold where they fine it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Iron is taken out of the earth, and brass is molten out of the stone.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "He setteth an end to darkness, and searcheth out all perfection: the stones of darkness, and the shadow of death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "The flood breaketh out from the inhabitant; even the waters forgotten of the foot: they are dried up, they are gone away from men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "As for the earth, out of it cometh bread: and under it is turned up as it were fire.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "The stones of it are the place of sapphires: and it hath dust of gold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "There is a path which no fowl knoweth, and which the vulture’s eye hath not seen:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The lion’s whelps have not trodden it, nor the fierce lion passed by it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He putteth forth his hand upon the rock; he overturneth the mountains by the roots.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He cutteth out rivers among the rocks; and his eye seeth every precious thing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "He bindeth the floods from overflowing; and the thing that is hid bringeth he forth to light.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "But where shall wisdom be found? and where is the place of understanding?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Man knoweth not the price thereof; neither is it found in the land of the living.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "The depth saith, It is not in me: and the sea saith, It is not with me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "It cannot be gotten for gold, neither shall silver be weighed for the price thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "It cannot be valued with the gold of Ophir, with the precious onyx, or the sapphire.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The gold and the crystal cannot equal it: and the exchange of it shall not be for jewels of fine gold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "No mention shall be made of coral, or of pearls: for the price of wisdom is above rubies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The topaz of Ethiopia shall not equal it, neither shall it be valued with pure gold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Whence then cometh wisdom? and where is the place of understanding?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Seeing it is hid from the eyes of all living, and kept close from the fowls of the air.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Destruction and death say, We have heard the fame thereof with our ears.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "God understandeth the way thereof, and he knoweth the place thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "For he looketh to the ends of the earth, and seeth under the whole heaven;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "To make the weight for the winds; and he weigheth the waters by measure.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "When he made a decree for the rain, and a way for the lightning of the thunder:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Then did he see it, and declare it; he prepared it, yea, and searched it out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:28:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "And unto man he said, Behold, the fear of the LORD, that is wisdom; and to depart from evil is understanding.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 28:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:28:28"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
